From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:55:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: Add Allwinner A733 deinterlace unit

The A733 has a deinterlace unit, the DI (manual section 14.4). Add its
binding, in media with the other memory-to-memory video engines.

The deinterlace unit of the H3, R40 and A64 has a binding of its own,
but it names a DRAM clock the A733 does not have, and its register
layout is not known to match, so the compatible does not fall back to
it. The A733 block sits in the DE_SYS power domain with the
display engine and has its bus master behind the second IOMMU (manual
chapter 10). The four clocks are the bus gate, the module clock, the
MBUS clock enable of the DE_SYS port and the AHB clock enable of the
display engine system (manual sections 4.1.6.107, 4.1.6.106, 4.1.6.83
and 4.1.6.82).

Not covered: the manual describes no register of the block, so nothing
register-level is described. The reset of DE_SYS itself is not taken: it
is de-asserted by default (manual section 4.1.6.113).

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled for a test, the
deinterlace unit probes with the four clocks, reset, power domain and
IOMMU master this binding names, and its register window answers while
the block is resumed.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml    | 87 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 87 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..25bb2e24c721
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Allwinner A733 Deinterlace Unit
+
+maintainers:
+  - Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
+
+description:
+  The deinterlace unit of the A733 converts interlaced video buffers in
+  memory to progressive ones, with weave and pixel-motion-adaptive
+  deinterlacing, temporal noise reduction and film-mode detection. It sits
+  in the display engine system (DE_SYS) beside the display engine, is
+  powered with it, and its bus master is behind the second IOMMU.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clocks:
+    items:
+      - description: Bus gate (DI_BGR_REG)
+      - description: Module clock (DI_CLK_REG)
+      - description: MBUS clock enable of the DE_SYS port
+      - description: AHB clock enable of the display engine system
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: bus
+      - const: mod
+      - const: mbus
+      - const: ahb
+
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  power-domains:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  iommus:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - clocks
+  - clock-names
+  - resets
+  - power-domains
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+
+    bus {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <1>;
+
+        deinterlace@5400000 {
+            compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-deinterlace";
+            reg = <0x05400000 0x40000>;
+            interrupts = <GIC_SPI 52 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+            clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_DI>, <&ccu CLK_DI>,
+                     <&ccu CLK_MBUS_DESYS>, <&ccu CLK_AHB_DE>;
+            clock-names = "bus", "mod", "mbus", "ahb";
+            resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_DI>;
+            power-domains = <&pck600 PD_DE_SYS>;
+            iommus = <&iommu1 3>;
+        };
+    };
+
+...
